# Wildfire Nowcast — A' pivot environment configuration
# Copy this file to .env.local for local dev, or set via Vercel dashboard
# (Preview + Production scopes) for deployments.
#
# Most secrets are not yet provisioned. See pm/blockers.md for the
# Vanyo-handoff queue (Neon, AI Gateway, Resend, Clerk, CRON_SECRET).
# The build-without-blocking pattern (ADR 0006) means routes return
# typed 503s when their dependencies are unset; the app still builds.

# =============================================================================
# Stage 1 — Postgres (Neon)
# =============================================================================
# Pooled connection string from Neon (host ending in `-pooler`). Required for
# the AOI route handlers; without it they return 503 service_unavailable.
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://USER:PASS@ep-xxx-pooler.eu-central-1.aws.neon.tech/wildfire-nowcast?sslmode=require

# =============================================================================
# Stage 2 — FIRMS poll + GitHub Actions cron
# =============================================================================
# NASA FIRMS API key. Free at https://firms.modaps.eosdis.nasa.gov/api/
FIRMS_MAP_KEY=your_firms_api_key_here

# Shared secret for the GitHub Actions FIRMS poll. Set on both Vercel
# (Preview + Production) and as a GitHub Actions repo secret. The
# /api/aoi/poll endpoint requires `Authorization: Bearer <CRON_SECRET>`.
# Generate with: `openssl rand -hex 32`
# CRON_SECRET=your_hex_cron_secret_here

# =============================================================================
# Stage 3 — Brief generation (Vercel AI Gateway) — pending
# =============================================================================
# Free tier includes $5/mo credit. Enable at Vercel dashboard → AI Gateway.
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# =============================================================================
# Stage 4 — Notifications (Resend) — pending
# =============================================================================
# Free tier: 3,000 emails/mo, 100/day. https://resend.com
# RESEND_API_KEY=

# Sender address for outbound notification email. MUST be on a verified
# Resend domain in production; otherwise prod ships from a placeholder
# default and lib/notify/resend.ts emits a misconfiguration warning.
# NOTIFY_FROM_ADDRESS=notifications@your-verified-domain.example

# =============================================================================
# Stage 5 — Auth (Clerk) — pending
# =============================================================================
# Free tier: 10,000 MAU. https://clerk.com
# The publishable key is exposed to the browser via the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix
# (Next.js convention); the secret key stays server-only.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=

# Svix-format signing secret for the Clerk webhook endpoint
# (/api/webhooks/clerk). Without it the route returns 503.
# Source: Clerk dashboard → Webhooks → endpoint signing key.
# CLERK_WEBHOOK_SIGNING_SECRET=

# =============================================================================
# Public app origin (build-time, baked into the client bundle)
# =============================================================================
# Canonical public URL used to format brief share links. Set to the deployed
# Vercel origin (no trailing slash). Because NEXT_PUBLIC_* is inlined at build
# time, changes require a redeploy.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://wildfire-nowcast.vercel.app
